    "body": "## Summary\n\nImplements **ADR-020: Page Caching for Back/Forward Navigation**. Back and Forward now serve from an in-memory session cache, so returning to a previously-visited page is instant instead of re-fetching.\n\nThis is the largest deferred item from ADR-019 — Back currently re-fetches, which is invisible on localhost but wrong on any real network.\n\nThree commits: PageCache data structure + tests, HoneyBeeWindow integration, docs.\n\n## Commits\n\n| Commit | Scope |\n|---|---|\n| `533162f` | `PageCache` class + 8 unit tests (header-only, no GTK) |\n| `7dc6d38` | `HoneyBeeWindow` integration: `m_cache` member, short-circuit for Back/Forward, populate on success, distinct status message |\n| `ff41860` | Docs: ADR status -> Implemented, README row, CHANGELOG |\n\n## Cache policy\n\n| NavKind | Cache read | Cache write | Verified |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `New` | no | yes (on success) | Step 7 |\n| `Back` | **yes** (skip fetch on hit) | yes (on success, i.e. on miss) | Step 4, 9 |\n| `Forward` | **yes** (skip fetch on hit) | yes (on success) | Step 5 |\n| `Reload` | no | yes (overwrites with fresh body) | Step 6, 8 |\n\nNew and Reload always fetch fresh — without HTTP cache headers, serving stale content on explicit navigation would be surprising. Both still populate the cache so a subsequent Back is instant.\n\n## Design highlights\n\n- **Cache short-circuit fires before fetch.** No \"جارٍ الجلب...\" status, no button-disable. Back feels instant because it is.\n- **Distinct status message** — `من الذاكرة، الحجم: N بايت` for cache hits vs `تم الجلب، الحجم: N بايت` for fetches. On localhost, hit and fetch are both instantaneous, so this text is the only reliable visual signal.\n- **`record_visit` still fires on cache hit** — needed for `RenderState::base_url` (relative-href resolution) and idempotent `visited_urls` updates. Proven: \"Go to page B\" stays purple on cached Back.\n- **Reload refreshes the cache entry** — the fetch success callback calls `m_cache.put` unconditionally, overwriting the previous body.\n- **No eviction** — unbounded in v1, which preserves the \"Back always hits\" invariant that ADR-019 relies on.\n\n## The definitive test: kill the HTTP server mid-session\n\nThis is the strongest verification of the three ADRs (018, 019, 020). It proves behavior that unit tests structurally cannot: **cache works when network is truly unavailable, AND cache is preferred when network is available**.\n\n### 9-step manual verification (all pass)\n\nSetup: server up, load A (363 bytes, cache miss), load B (150 bytes, cache miss).\n\n| # | Action | Status bar | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 3 | Kill HTTP server, curl confirms down | — | server unreachable |\n| 4 | **Back to A** | `من الذاكرة، 363 بايت` | **cache hit, server DOWN** |\n| 5 | **Forward to B** | `من الذاكرة، 150 بايت` | **cache hit, per-URL keying proven by byte count** |\n| 6 | **Reload on B** | `فشل الجلب، رمز الحالة: 0` | **cache bypassed, fetch failed** |\n| 7 | **New nav to A via URL bar** | `فشل الجلب، رمز الحالة: 0`, URL bar restored to B | **cache bypassed on New** |\n| 8 | Restart server, Reload on B | `تم الجلب، 150 بايت` | fetch succeeds, cache refreshed |\n| 9 | **Back to A (server UP)** | `من الذاكرة، 363 بايت` | **cache preferred over fetch** |\n\n**Why Steps 4 and 9 together are decisive:**\n- Step 4 alone proves \"cache works when server is unreachable\" — but that could be a fallback-only implementation.\n- Step 9 (server UP, cache hit still wins) proves cache is *preferred* over fetch, ruling out the fallback-only hypothesis.\n- Steps 6 and 7 prove the complementary case: Reload and New correctly *bypass* cache and fail when server is down.\n\nCombined, all four `NavKind` paths are empirically verified against real network conditions.\n\n## Test count\n\n- Unit: 8 new cases in `[page-cache]` (26 assertions), plus 245 existing\n- Total: **253 cases, 986 assertions**, all pass\n- Zero warnings\n- Visual verification: 9 states confirmed via the kill-server test\n\n## Deferred (future ADRs)\n\n- **Eviction / LRU / size cap** — unbounded in v1; interacts with the \"Back always hits\" invariant\n- **Persistence** across sessions\n- **HTTP cache semantics** (`Cache-Control`, `ETag`, `Vary`)\n- **Conditional GETs** (`If-Modified-Since`, `If-None-Match`)\n- **Bfcache-style page state** — form values, JS state, scroll position\n- **Cache invalidation on POST** (no POST in v1)\n\n## ADR\n\n`docs/decisions/020-page-cache.md` — status now **Implemented**.\n",
